course: dictionary
lesson: 14299
title: A novice is a beginner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A novice is someone who is new to something and has not had much practice yet. Novice is a noun, and it can also be an adjective, as in «a novice skier». The clue to look for is a person who is just starting out and still learning.
explain: Context gives you the clues. «Sam had never held a chess piece before, so he was a complete novice.» Sam is new and has never played, so novice means beginner. If you swap in beginner and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: The word has two other uses. In a church, a novice is someone training to become a monk or nun. In sport and competitions, a novice class is one for people who are beginners. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: A novice is a beginner, someone new to an activity.
fact: A novice has little skill or experience yet.
fact: The opposite of a novice is an expert.
fact: In a church, a novice is a trainee monk or nun, who has not yet made their final promises.
fact: «Novice level» in a club or competition means the class is for beginners.
exercise: «Mia had only ever swum twice, so she was a novice in the pool.» What is a novice? | An expert with many medals | *A beginner | A teacher | A lifeguard
exercise: «The novice chess club meets on Tuesdays for players who are just learning.» What does novice mean here? | For very old players | *For beginners | A famous chess player | A club that is closed
exercise: Which word is the opposite of novice? | *Expert | Beginner | Student | Trainee
test: «Jake built his first robot last week, and he is still a novice at coding.» What does novice mean? | A robot maker | Someone who has finished all the lessons | An expert at coding | *Someone new who is still learning
test: In a church, a novice is someone who | has left the church forever | *is training to become a monk or nun | is the leader of the church | is the oldest member of the choir
exam: What does novice mean in «Ruby was a novice rider, so her teacher held the horse steady.»? | A teacher who is very strict | *A beginner who is still learning | A famous horse | A rider who has won many prizes
